{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5614c581-7ba5-4cf0-8218-e91da1bba194",
    "name": "Go Data Pipeline",
    "description": "Updated against go-pipeline-postgres-docker-full-project.zip. Start Docker Compose first and set collection variables baseUrl and apiKey (matches API_KEY in .env). Run folders 01 and 02 in order, then 03 for negative tests. The Poll request loops in Collection Runner until the job finishes; for individual Send requests, poll manually. Folder 04 contains optional/manual tests and may delete job data; do not include it in an ordinary full-run. PostgreSQL itself is not a REST endpoint: persistence verification requires restarting the API container before rerunning the saved-job requests. Docker uses INPUT_DIR=/app/testdata/input, so the sample paths are testdata/input/customers.csv and customers.json; the exports are confined to output/<job-id>/ and are ephemeral under the current Docker Compose tmpfs.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
